I would add my voice to Michal Jaegermann's and state my dislike for
the nf filename prefix. I have about 6000 files using a times.sty style
option.

Originally times.sty was my own hacky extension of NFSS. I then
replaced it with spqr's PSNFSS.  Significantly, changes to the LaTeX
system could be made without altering the contents to the document.
Although the interface has changed slightly with NFSS2, nevertheless
most documents can be processed unchanged except for the style options
line.

So it seems undesirable to change a document just because a style name
has changed.

